            <ArticleTitle>A case report of the new Polyzene™-F COBRA PzF™ Nanocoated Coronary Stent System (NCS): Addressing an unmet clinical need.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>209-11</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.carrev.2016.01.007</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1553-8389(16)30004-5</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Because of anticipated antiplatelet medication risks, patients who are not DES candidates or who are at particularly high risk for bleeding events have been targeted initially for treatment with the COBRA PzF Coronary Stent System. We report the case of a successful experience with a new, Polyzene™-F COBRA PzF™ Coronary Stent System, designed to impart thrombo-resistance and reduce inflammation, to achieve shorter dual antiplatelet therapy duration while reducing restenosis incidence in a high risk patient with atrial fibrillation.</AbstractText>
